From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 02:23:22 +0200
Subject: media: ov5640: Fix autofocus start/stop and status readback

The four focus controls were put in a plain cluster, so the control
framework always called s_ctrl with the cluster master (FOCUS_AUTO).
The AUTO_FOCUS_START and AUTO_FOCUS_STOP cases were never reached and
triggering a single focus did nothing but re-apply the continuous
focus setting.

AUTO_FOCUS_STATUS was not marked volatile either. The framework only
computes has_volatiles from the cluster members, so g_volatile_ctrl
was never called and userspace always read back the cached IDLE.

Drop the cluster, the controls are independent, and mark the status
control volatile so it is read from the firmware on every get.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
@@ -3624,7 +3624,7 @@ static int ov5640_g_volatile_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 			return val;
 		sensor->ctrls.exposure->val = val;
 		break;
-	case V4L2_CID_FOCUS_AUTO:
+	case V4L2_CID_AUTO_FOCUS_STATUS:
 		val = ov5640_get_af_status(sensor);
 		if (val < 0)
 			return val;
@@ -3846,11 +3846,11 @@ static int ov5640_init_controls(struct ov5640_dev *sensor)
 	ctrls->vblank->flags |= V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_READ_ONLY;
 	ctrls->gain->flags |= V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_VOLATILE;
 	ctrls->exposure->flags |= V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_VOLATILE;
+	ctrls->af_status->flags |= V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_VOLATILE;
 
 	v4l2_ctrl_auto_cluster(3, &ctrls->auto_wb, 0, false);
 	v4l2_ctrl_auto_cluster(2, &ctrls->auto_gain, 0, true);
 	v4l2_ctrl_auto_cluster(2, &ctrls->auto_exp, 1, true);
-	v4l2_ctrl_cluster(4, &ctrls->focus_auto);
 
 	sensor->sd.ctrl_handler = hdl;
 	return 0;
